      "problem": "Find the value of $\\sqrt{3x+5y}$ when $x=1$ and $y=5.$",
      "worked_solution": "We replace $x$ with $1$ and $y$ with $5$ in the given expression, and simplify as much as possible:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{3x+5y} & = \\\\ \\sqrt{3(1)+5(5)} & = \\\\ \\sqrt{3+25} & = \\\\ \\sqrt{28} & = \\\\ \\sqrt{4\\cdot 7} & = \\\\ \\sqrt{{2}^{2}\\cdot 7} & = \\\\ \\sqrt{{2}^{2}}\\cdot \\sqrt{7} & = \\\\ 2\\sqrt{7}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
